Z||000000||Sevaan||03-19-2001||10:14 PM||||What are some cool, cheap and easy mods that one can do to their Fiero (without spending a boatload of money?)<P>I'm talking about small things, like painting little bits here and there that add up to a whole.<P>What do you suggest?||||reg||1
Z||000001||85Josh||03-19-2001||10:18 PM||||Get a set of Oreif's door emblems, just $5 and they really look great.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Fierowrecker||03-19-2001||10:27 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Sevaan:<BR><B>What are some cool, cheap and easy mods that one can do to their Fiero (without spending a boatload of money?)<P>I'm talking about small things, like painting little bits here and there that add up to a whole.<P>What do you suggest?</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>I would pick up a few bug bombs at NAPA of their semi-gloss trim paint and do the mirrors, deck lid trim, wing, bumpers, what ever is black on the outside...<BR>This adds a lot of NEW look to your car without doing a full paint job...<BR>Chances are, your headliner is sagging...<BR>Pick up a can of spray adhesive and new headliner material from JCWhitney...<BR>If you have alloy wheels, clean em up!<BR>Most improvements are elbow grease stuff, like shampooing the interior, and Whestlies bleach-white on the tires...<BR>Then Armor-all the tires and dash...<BR>DETAILS!<BR>That's why they call it detailing!||||reg||1
Z||000003||Cheever2||03-19-2001||10:37 PM||||Here's what Forum members <B>wanted</B> for Christmas...<BR> <A HREF="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum6/HTML/001033.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum6/HTML/001033.html</A> <P>This was what they <B>got</B> for Christmas.  Some of this is Fiero related, some isn't, but it's fun to look back on it…<BR> <A HREF="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum6/HTML/001145.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum6/HTML/001145.html</A> <P>I've seen pics of some cars with white face gauges, and think they look great.<P><p>[This message has been edited by Cheever2 (edited 03-19-2001).]||||reg||6
Z||000004||LottaBallsCamaro||03-19-2001||10:54 PM||||Fierowrecker pretty much covered it. A good tune up and a K&N air filter could make a big difference depending on how bad, if at all, it needs it. Sure it wont make your Fiero look better but you cant really see a car very could when it passes you doign 200MPH!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>------------------<BR>91'RS 305TBI no mods to date<BR>92' Lumina 275,000 miles and still humping!!!!||||reg||1
